\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces Experimental sequence for the magnetic field, laser intensities, and laser frequencies as a function of time, spanning the blue MOT through to time-of-flight imaging. \textbf  {Top:} magnetic field gradient (BMOT) and the three bias/compensation coil voltages (VA, VC, VD). \textbf  {Middle:} intensities of the $461~$nm, $403~$nm, $689~$nm, and $1064~$nm light. \textbf  {Bottom:} frequency detunings of the MOT and STIR (stirring) beams during the broadband/SWAP and narrowband stages, and of the reservoir/dimple beams during evaporation. The bottom right inset details the imaging sequence (probe, reference, and dark exposures). AOM drive amplitudes still awaiting final calibration are highlighted.}}{7}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
